<title>OMAN: Oman's GDP rises 10.7 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Oman's GDP rises 10.7 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MUSCAT 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman's gross domestic product (GDP) at market prices rose 10.7 percent to 5.85 billion rials in 1996, provisional Ministry of Development figures show. Contribution to GDP by sectors in millions of rials:</p>
<p>							1996	    1995</p>
<p>Petroleum activities</p>
<p>Crude petroleum				  2,431.7     1,974.1</p>
<p>Natural gas					 49.0	    46.8</p>
<p>Total petroleum activities		 2,480.8	 2,021.0</p>
<p>Non-petroleum activities</p>
<p> Mining and quarrying			   15.8	    17.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing				   253.7	   240.8</p>
<p> Electricity and water			  50.3	    49.1</p>
<p> Building and construction		   130.1	   137.6</p>
<p> Wholesale and retail trade		  719.6	   671.5</p>
<p> Public administration and defence	 714.3	   705.6</p>
<p> Other activities			    1,603.9	 1,531.8</p>
<p>Total non-petroleum activities	   3,487.7	 3,353.5</p>
<p>Financial intermediation		    (157.0)	 (131.6)</p>
<p>Customs duties				    43.1	    45.3</p>
<p>GDP at market prices			 5,854.5	 5,288.2</p>
<p>1996 figures are provisional. 1995 figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>Note: Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
</text>
